# __PROJECT_NAME__ agent guide

AGENTS.md is a symlink to this file. Keep code, documentation, comments and agent instructions in English.
Read .agents/skills/project/SKILL.md, and the Maximus skill in .agents/skills/maximus/SKILL.md, a link into
node_modules/@arbol-ai/maximus that `bun install` fills.

## Structure

This is a Maximus project on Cloudflare Workers. vite.config.ts is its only configuration: maximus() states
the application, its bindings and its Worker, and errors.ts, context.ts, auth.ts and telemetry.ts complete
it in code when present.

- routes/: one defineHandler(handler, contract) per file, named by its path and method:
  routes/v1/tasks/[taskId].delete.ts answers DELETE /api/v1/tasks/{taskId}. Its operation name, effect and
  scope derive from the method and path unless declared. Declare strict input and output schemas, and MCP
  or RPC exposure explicitly.
- mcp/tools/: tools only MCP serves, one defineTool per kebab-case file. mcp/instructions.md, mcp/guides/
  and mcp/skills/ describe the MCP server to every client, so they hold no tenant data.
- middleware/: defineMiddleware wraps requests before token admission and sees no principal;
  defineOperationMiddleware runs after admission on HTTP, MCP and RPC. Modules run in filename order.
- pages/: public responses at fixed paths outside the API, for GET unless the file names its method:
  pages/webhooks/payments.post.ts receives a provider's webhook and verifies its signature itself. They hold
  no tenant data.
- index.html, app/ and public/: a web app, when index.html exists. app/routes/ holds its React Router
  pages, named as routes are, and the app calls the API with fetch and the person's token.
- crons/: scheduled handlers, each exporting its schedule as `export const cron = '…'`. queues/: one
  consumer per queue, named after it. email/: one handler per recipient address, and _default.
  durable-objects/: Durable Object classes, day-schedule.ts exported as DaySchedule.
- src/: shared domain code. tests/: tests that call `handler` from #maximus/http in Node.
- .maximus/: generated by `maximus prepare`, vp dev, vp build and vp test. Never edit it, and never import
  it at runtime from errors.ts, context.ts, auth.ts or telemetry.ts.

The project-structure guide maps every file:
https://github.com/getarbol/maximus/blob/main/docs/guides/project-structure.md. Bindings and triggers
belong in maximus(); Env is generated from them. Creating Cloudflare resources and applying migrations stay
explicit: adding a file never provisions anything.

## Boundaries

Tenant authority is the verified principal's organizationId, never caller input. Answer expected failures
with `fail(code)` from errors.ts, declared in the route's `failures`. Never put credentials, personal or
clinical data or request bodies in logs, examples, errors or agent instructions. Secrets are
bindings.secret(); .dev.vars is local and ignored by Git. A deployed Worker accepts only the access tokens
of tokens.issuer, so set it to the real authorization server before deploying.

## Workflows

`bun run dev` runs the Worker locally and `bun run test` runs the tests. `bun run verify` runs type
generation, TypeScript, lint and format, the tests and the build; CI runs it on every pull request. Use
`cf` for Cloudflare: discover commands with `cf cli search` and inspect a command's API request with
`cf schema` before running it. Deploy with `bun run deploy` or the GitHub workflow. Preserve unrelated work
and Git identity configuration, and add no assistant attribution to commits.
